// ============================================================================
// VendTable.update() modification – add to existing VendTable table class
// ============================================================================
// PURPOSE
// -------
// Intercepts VendTable updates and records a pending-removal entry when a
// vendor's BT_VendApprovalStatusId changes FROM an approved/preferred status
// to a non-approved status.
//
// HOW TO APPLY
// ------------
// In AOT > Data Dictionary > Tables > VendTable > Methods > update(),
// add the following call AT THE END of the existing method, after super():
//
//   // BT Customisation: CDX vendor-approval change tracking.
//   BT_CDXVendorApprovalChangeHandler::onVendTableUpdated(orig, this);
//
// Full method skeleton after modification:
// ============================================================================

// [In VendTable.update() – add the marked lines]
public void update()
{
    VendTable orig;

    // ---- EXISTING CODE: capture original before super() ------------------
    // (This pattern is already present in most AX2012 VendTable overrides.
    //  If orig is already captured elsewhere in the method, reuse that.)
    select firstonly orig
        where orig.RecId == this.RecId;
    // ---- END EXISTING CODE -----------------------------------------------

    super(); // Standard AX update logic

    // ---- BT CUSTOMISATION: CDX approval-change tracking ------------------
    // If the vendor's approval status changed FROM approved/preferred to
    // something else, record a pending-removal entry so that the next CDX
    // incremental run can re-sync this vendor (with non-approved status)
    // to all active EPOS channels.
    BT_CDXVendorApprovalChangeHandler::onVendTableUpdated(orig, this);
    // ---- END BT CUSTOMISATION --------------------------------------------
}

// ============================================================================
// IMPORTANT NOTES
// ============================================================================
//
// 1. "orig" capture pattern
//    If VendTable.update() already selects the original record for other
//    customisations, reuse that buffer (do not select twice).
//    A common pattern is:
//
//      VendTable origVendTable = VendTable::find(this.AccountNum);
//
//    Replace "orig" above with whatever buffer name is already in use.
//
// 2. Performance
//    BT_CDXVendorApprovalChangeHandler::onVendTableUpdated() checks
//    whether the status field actually changed before doing any DB work,
//    so the overhead on updates that don't change the status is minimal
//    (one field comparison + return).
//
// 3. Bulk updates via doUpdate() / update_recordset
//    If any background process updates BT_VendApprovalStatusId via
//    update_recordset or doUpdate() (which bypass the update() method),
//    you must also call BT_CDXVendorApprovalChangeHandler manually in
//    that code, or replace the bulk statement with a record-by-record loop
//    wrapped in tts.
//
// 4. Delete scenario
//    If a vendor is deleted entirely (VendTable.delete()), a similar
//    pattern should be applied in VendTable.delete() using a dedicated
//    delete handler.  Deletions are typically handled by the CDX schema's
//    delete-tracking mechanism, but you should verify this for your schema.
// ============================================================================
